{
  "title": "75: Al-Qiyamah القيامة",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِيَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِۙ‏(1)\nLAA UQSEMO BE-YAWMIL QEYAAMAH.\nI swear by the Day of Resurrection!\nوَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِالنَّفْسِ اللَّوَّامَةِؕ‏(2)\nWA LAA UQSEMO BIN-NAFSIL LAWWAAMAH.\nAnd I swear by the self-critical soul!\nاَيَحْسَبُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَلَّنْ نَّجْمَعَ عِظَامَهٗؕ‏(3)\nAYAHSABUL INSAANO ALLAN NAJMA-A’ E’ZAAMAH.\nDoes man suppose that We will not put together his bones [at resurrection]?\nبَلٰى قٰدِرِيْنَ عَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّسَوِّىَ بَنَانَهٗ‏(4)\nBALAA QAADEREENA A’LAA AN NOSAWWEYA BANAANAH.\nYes indeed, We are able to [re]shape [even] his fingertips!\nبَلْ يُرِيْدُ الْاِنْسَانُ لِيَفْجُرَ اَمَامَهٗ‌ۚ‏(5)\nBAL YOREEDUL INSAANO LE-YAFJORA AMAAMAH.\nIndeed, man desires to go on living viciously.\nيَسْئَلُ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ‏(6)\nYAS-ALO AYYAANA YAWMUL QEYAAMAH.\nHe asks, ‘When will be this “day of resurrection”?!’\nفَاِذَا بَرِقَ الْبَصَرُۙ‏(7)\nFA-EZAA BAREQAL BASAR.\nBut when the eyes are dazzled,\nوَخَسَفَ الْقَمَرُۙ‏(8)\nWA KHASAFAL QAMAR.\nthe moon is eclipsed,\nوَجُمِعَ الشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُۙ‏(9)\nWA JOME-A’SH SHAMSO WAL QAMAR.\nand the sun and the moon are brought together,\nيَقُوْلُ الْاِنْسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍ اَيْنَ الْمَفَرُّ‌ ۚ‏(10)\nYAQOOLUL INSAANO YAWMA-EZIN AYNAL MAFAR.\nthat day man will say, ‘Where is the escape [from this day]?’\nكَلَّا لَا وَزَرَؕ‏(11)\nKALLAA LAA WAZAR.\nNo indeed! There will be no refuge!\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْمُسْتَقَرُّ ؕ‏(12)\nELAA RABBEKA YAWMA-EZENIL MUSTAQAR.\nThat day the [final] goal will be toward your Lord.\nيُنَبَّؤُا الْاِنْسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَ وَاَخَّرَؕ‏(13)\nYONABBA-UL INSAANO YAWMA-EZIM BEMAA QADDAMA WA AKH-KHAR.\nThat day man will be informed about what [works] he had sent ahead [to the scene of judgement] and [the legacy that he had] left behind.\nبَلِ الْاِنْسَانُ عَلٰى نَفْسِهٖ بَصِيْرَةٌ ۙ‏(14)\nBALIL INSAANO A’LAA NAFSEHI BASEERAH.\nIndeed, man is a witness to himself,\nوَّلَوْ اَلْقٰى مَعَاذِيْرَهٗؕ‏(15)\nWA LAW ALQAA MA-A’AZEERAH.\nthough he should offer excuses [to justify his failings].\nلَا تُحَرِّكْ بِهٖ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهٖؕ‏(16)\nLAA TOHARRIK BEHI LESAANAKA LE-TA’JALA BEH.\nDo not move your tongue with it to hasten it.\nاِنَّ عَلَيْنَا جَمْعَهٗ وَقُرْاٰنَهٗۚ  ۖ‏(17)\nINNA A’LAYNAA JAM-A’HU WA QUR-AANAH.\nIndeed it is up to Us to put it together and to recite it.\nفَاِذَا قَرَاْنٰهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْاٰنَهٗ‌ۚ‏(18)\nFA-EZAA QARAANAAHO FAT-TABE’ QUR-AANAH.\nAnd when We have recited it, follow its recitation.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ عَلَيْنَا بَيَانَهٗؕ‏(19)\nSUMMA INNA A’LAYNAA BAYAANAH.\nThen, its exposition [also] lies with Us.\nكَلَّا بَلْ تُحِبُّوْنَ الْعَاجِلَةَ ۙ‏(20)\nKALLAA BAL TOHIBBOONAL A’AJELAH.\nNo! Indeed, you love this transitory life\nوَتَذَرُوْنَ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ‏(21)\nWA TAZAROONAL AAKHERAH.\nand forsake the Hereafter.\nوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ نَّاضِرَةٌ ۙ‏(22)\nWOJOOHUN-Y YAWMA-EZIN NAAZERAH.\nSome faces will be fresh on that day,\nاِلٰى رَبِّهَا نَاظِرَةٌ‌ ۚ‏(23)\nELAA RABBEHAA NAAZERAH.\nlooking to their Lord,\nوَوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍۢ بَاسِرَةٌ ۙ‏(24)\nWA WOJOOHUN-Y YAWMA-EZIM BAASERAH.\nand some faces will be scowling on that day,\nتَظُنُّ اَنْ يُّفْعَلَ بِهَا فَاقِرَةٌ ؕ‏(25)\nTAZUNNO AN-Y YUF-A’LA BEHAA FAAQERAH.\nknowing that they will be dealt out a punishment breaking the spine.\nكَلَّاۤ اِذَا بَلَغَتِ التَّرَاقِىَۙ‏(26)\nKALLAA EZAA BALAGHATIT TARAAQEE.\nNo indeed! When it reaches up to the collar bones\nوَقِيْلَ مَنْ رَاقٍۙ‏(27)\nWA QEELA MAN  RAAQ.\nand it is said, ‘Who will take him up?’\nوَّظَنَّ اَنَّهُ الْفِرَاقُۙ‏(28)\nWA ZANNA ANNAHUL FERAAQ.\nand he knows that it is the [time of] parting,\nوَالْتَفَّتِ السَّاقُ بِالسَّاقِۙ‏(29)\nWAL TAFFATIS SAAQO BIS-SAAQ.\nand each shank clasps the other shank,\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْمَسَاقُؕ‏(30)\nELAA RABBEKA YAWMA-EZENIL MASAAQ.\nthat day he shall be driven toward your Lord.\nفَلَا صَدَّقَ وَلَا صَلّٰىۙ‏(31)\nFALAA SADDAQA WA LAA SALLAA.\nHe neither confirmed [the messages of Allah], nor did he pray,\nوَلٰكِنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىۙ‏(32)\nWA LAAKIN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nbut denied [them] and turned away,\nثُمَّ ذَهَبَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ يَتَمَطّٰىؕ‏(33)\nSUMMA ZAHABA ELAA AHLEHI YATAMATTAA.\nand went back swaggering to his family.\nاَوْلٰى لَكَ فَاَوْلٰىۙ‏(34)\nAWLAA LAKA FA-AWLAA.\nSo, woe to you! Woe to you!\nثُمَّ اَوْلٰى لَكَ فَاَوْلٰىؕ‏(35)\nSUMMA AWLAA LAKA FA-AWLAA.\nAgain, woe to you! Woe to you!\nاَيَحْسَبُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَنْ يُّتْرَكَ سُدًىؕ‏(36)\nAYAHSABUL INSAANO AN-Y YUTRAKA SODAA.\nDoes man suppose that he has been abandoned to futility?\nاَلَمْ يَكُ نُطْفَةً مِّنْ مَّنِىٍّ يُّمْنٰىۙ‏(37)\nALAM YAKO NUTFATAM MIM MANIYYIN-Y YUMNAA.\nWas he not a drop of emitted semen,\nثُمَّ كَانَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقَ فَسَوّٰىۙ‏(38)\nSUMMA KAANA A’LAQATAN FA-KHALAQA FA-SAWWAA.\nand then a clinging mass? Whereat He created and proportioned [him],\nفَجَعَلَ مِنْهُ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰىؕ‏(39)\nFA-JA-A’LA MINHUZ ZAWJAYNIZ ZAKARA WAL UNSAA.\nand made of him the two sexes, male and female.\nاَلَيْسَ ذٰلِكَ بِقٰدِرٍ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يُّحْىِۦَ الْمَوْتٰى‏(40)\nALAYSA ZAALEKA BE-QAADERIN A’LAA AN-Y YOHYAL MAWTAA.\nIs not [someone like] that able to revive the dead?",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qeyaamah (The Resurrection)\nThis Surah has 40 verses and it is ‘Makki’. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites this Surah will be counted from among those who believed in the Day of Judgement and his face will be shining when he is raised from his grave. It is also narrated that frequent reciters will be raised with handsome and attractive faces on the Day of Judgement.\nRecitation of this Surah increases sustenance and protects the life and possessions of the reciter. He is liked by people. Surah al-Qeyaamah also makes a person chaste, humble and sincere. Drinking water in which this Surah has been written keeps the heart safe from ailments."
}
